I have a suggestion to make regarding all these nethack patches.  Would it
be possible to make successive patches supersets of previous ones and make
them relative to the last full source version?

It seems that every patch that has gone out has had problems after release.
This is not a criticism of the developers, since I realize how large the
program has become and how many different contributors there were.  Because
I had to make corrections after both patches 1 and 2, and because I heard
about problems with patch 3 even before I had a chance to apply it, I am
still running at patch level 2.  Now I have to decide whether to install
patch 3, fix its problems, install patch 4, and fix its problems, or just
wait for the next full release.  I think I'll do the latter.

This difficulty could be overcome simply by making new patches fix all
known bugs in previous releases and requiring that any and all new patches
be applied to V3.0.  It would be a whole lot easier than trying to create
the thing in incremental steps.  I suppose this would be a problem for
people who didn't archive 3.0, but maybe a "reversal" patch could be
distributed to generate a 3.0 archive from the previous patch level.

I appreciate the work being done to fix bugs and make enhancements,
but the user interface is getting pretty unfriendly.

